## Executive Overview

The **Conformal Cosmic Funnel & Lens Framework** proposes a non-singular model for stellar collapse past the Tolman-Oppenheimer-Volkoff (TOV) limit. By generalizing the Kerr spacetime metric in Boyer-Lindquist coordinates, this framework demonstrates how relativistic angular momentum ($J_\phi$) and negative radial pressure ($P_r$) prevent gravitational collapse to a singular density point ($r = 0$).

Rather than terminating in a classical black hole singularity, infalling matter is channeled through a dynamically open, stabilized metric throat into an independent, expanding child spacetime. At the decoupling boundary ($z \sim 1100$), an **Isotropic Lens Operator** ($A_{\text{lens}}$) converts localized vector rotation into a homogeneous scalar pressure field, driving uniform cosmic expansion.

