## Key Mathematical Foundations

### 1. Kerr Metric & Ergosphere Mechanics
Static boundaries are replaced with a stationary, axisymmetric Kerr metric template in Boyer-Lindquist coordinates:

$$ds^{2}=-\left(1-\frac{2Mr}{\rho^{2}}\right)dt^{2}-\left(\frac{4Mar\sin^{2}\theta}{\rho^{2}}\right)dtd\phi+\left(\frac{\rho^{2}}{\Delta}\right)dr^{2}+\rho^{2}d\theta^{2}+\left(r^{2}+a^{2}+\frac{2Ma^{2}r\sin^{2}\theta}{\rho^{2}}\right)\sin^{2}\theta d\phi^{2}$$

*(where $\rho^{2}=r^{2}+a^{2}\cos^{2}\theta$ and $\Delta=r^{2}-2Mr+a^{2}$)*

The invariant spin parameter $a = J/M$ establishes an ergosphere bounded by $r_+ = M + \sqrt{M^2 - a^2}$. Relativistic frame dragging forces infalling matter into a high-velocity rotational ring configuration, preventing static collapse.

### 2. Upgraded Stress-Energy Tensor Pipeline
Mass accretion across the horizon boundary is governed by an expanded stress-energy tensor:

$$T_{\mu\nu}^{\text{injected}} = (P_{\text{pipeline}} + P_\phi) u_\mu u_\nu + P_r g_{\mu\nu} + J_\phi$$

* **$P_{\text{pipeline}}$**: Incoming accreted mass energy density.
* **$P_\phi$**: Azimuthal kinetic pressure.
* **$J_\phi$**: Conserved angular momentum, preserved due to zero vacuum drag.
* **$P_r$**: Negative radial pressure acting as outward structural tension.

### 3. Singularity Avoidance via Centrifugal Repulsion
The geodesic equation incorporates repulsive centrifugal acceleration terms ($\Phi_{\text{centrifugal}}$):

$$\frac{d^2 x^\mu}{d\lambda^2} + \Gamma^\mu_{\alpha\beta}\frac{dx^\alpha}{d\lambda}\frac{dx^\beta}{d\lambda} - \Phi_{\text{centrifugal}} = 0$$

Because $T_{\phi\phi}$ cannot decay in vacuum, higher-power inverse scaling forces infalling geodesics to diverge before reaching $r = 0$. The negative radial pressure $P_r$ breaches the **Strong Energy Condition (SEC)**, maintaining a permanently open "funnel throat".

### 4. The Isotropic Lens Transformation ($A_{\text{lens}}$)
At the child universe decoupling boundary ($z \sim 1100$), the geometric diffuser function $A_{\text{lens}}$ transforms directional equatorial rotation into isotropic inflation:

$$\lim_{[r\to 0,\, z\to 1100]} \left[ A_{\text{lens}} \left( J_\phi \otimes P_r \right) \right] \longrightarrow \rho_{\text{isotropic\_expansion}}$$

This scrambles directional vector momentum into a uniform scalar driving pressure across the child cosmic web fabric.

